Author: Craig Hair <craig.hair@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Jul 12 21:41:28 2026 +1000

    macOS Kerberos: New-OpenADSessionOption -TargetSpnHost + optional GSSAPI/krb5 lib override
    
    Two STMC-local patches on top of v0.7.0-stmc1:
    - New-OpenADSessionOption -TargetSpnHost: decouples the Kerberos SPN host (ldap/<fqdn>, the DC's
      registered SPN) from the TCP -ComputerName, so you can connect by IP and still authenticate
      against the DC's SPN when the FQDN is unresolvable (VPN / no DNS). Session.cs
      OpenADSessionOptions.TargetSpnHost + cmdlet param + OpenADSessionFactory spnHost selection.
    - PSOPENAD_GSSAPI_LIB / PSOPENAD_KRB5_LIB env override in OnImportAndRemove: optionally load a
      specific native GSS/krb5 (e.g. MIT krb5) ahead of the system default. Dormant unless set.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/PSOpenAD.Module/Commands/OpenADSessionOption.cs b/src/PSOpenAD.Module/Commands/OpenADSessionOption.cs
